  "details": "SDK version: Avatars 3.8.0\n\nDescription of the bug: If a physbone component has its Root Transform set to an object that is *not on the avatar*, and there are no physbones in that object's hierarchy, exceptions get thrown by the SDK.\n\nIt tries to create a list with a capacity of -1.\n\nExceptions wind up getting thrown on every single editor update, which can break the editor interface (e.g. I couldn't change the root transform property!)\n\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\n\n1. Add a physbone to an avatar\n\n2. Add an empty game object to the scene (that is not parented to the avatar)\n\n3. Target that object with the physbone\n\n4. Open the control panel so that the SDK tries to check the avatar's performance stats.\n\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots): No",
